],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,5,8,5]],"output":[[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,2,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"The rule I found: **the two 5-coloured markers say how to cut the grid in half and which half to keep.**\n\n**Reading the markers.** Every input has exactly two cells of colour 5, two apart on a border. Every output is half the input, with the 5s erased.\n\n- **Pair 1:** the 5s are at (0,0) and (2,0). They are stacked vertically, so the height is halved. They sit in the top half, and the output is rows 0–9.\n- **Pair 2:** the 5s are at (0,9) and (2,9). Again vertical, so the height is halved, and they are in the top half. The output matches the crop at (0,0) of size 10×10.\n- **Pair 3:** the 5s are at (13,0) and (15,0). Vertical, but in the bottom half. Rows 8–15 of the input read left-pattern, right-pattern, left, right, left, then three empty rows. That is exactly the 8×30 output. It is not the top half, which would start with two empty rows.\n- **Pair 4:** the 5s are at (0,0) and (0,2). They lie side by side, so the width is halved. They are in the left half, and the output is columns 0–10, i.e. only the left block of 4s.\n\n**So the rule is:**\n1. The direction the marker pair runs picks the axis to halve.\n2. The half that contains the markers is kept.\n3. The 5s are replaced by the background colour.\n\n**On the tests:**\n- **Test 1:** the 5s are at (0,5) and (0,7). They are horizontal, in the right half, so the output is columns 4–7 (4×4) with the 5s erased.\n- **Test 2:** the 5s are at (9,25) and (9,27). They are horizontal, in the right half, so the output is columns 14–27 (10×14) with the 5s erased.\n\nThe emitted stages are: first erase the markers on the full canvas, then show the kept half.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    pts = list(zip(*np.where(g == 5)))\n    ys = [p[0] for p in pts]; xs = [p[1] for p in pts]\n    H, W = g.shape\n    clean = g.copy()\n    clean[g == 5] = bg\n    emit(clean, \"Erase the two 5-coloured markers, replacing them with background.\")\n    if len(set(xs)) == 1:  # markers stacked vertically -> halve height\n        h = H // 2\n        if min(ys) >= h:\n            out = clean[h:, :]\n            msg = \"Markers run vertically and lie in the bottom half: keep the bottom half.\"\n        else:\n            out = clean[:h, :]\n            msg = \"Markers run vertically and lie in the top half: keep the top half.\"\n    else:  # markers side by side -> halve width\n        w = W // 2\n        if min(xs) >= w:\n            out = clean[:, w:]\n            msg = \"Markers run horizontally and lie in the right half: keep the right half.\"\n        else:\n            out = clean[:, :w]\n            msg = \"Markers run horizontally and lie in the left half: keep the left half.\"\n    out = out.copy()\n    emit(out, msg)\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The output matches the crop at (0,0) of size 10×10."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"07bfcd00adce8e5bfcaa901aa6b3a0017daf185314093b332f154a2c05abee6c","task_sha256":"6da8ce6672ff4b54f4542a60b9efa314a21cb98db02924b44a683db8174cc041","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
